# An attribute's seed is for the instance variable it declares, which is
# not always one named after it:
# - `self.` makes it the class object's attribute (`class << self;
#   attr_accessor`), whose variable is the class's, not an instance's: no
#   seed (the seed format has no class-level variable)
# - `()` says it has no variable at all: no seed
# - `(@raw)` names the variable: the seed is for @raw
class AttrIvars
  attr_accessor self.dflt: String
  attr_reader self.count: Integer
  attr_reader computed (): Integer
  attr_reader parsed (@raw): String
  attr_accessor plain: Integer
  @explicit: Float
end
